<title>UK: FT-SE Eurotrack adds four companies, deletes four.</title>
<headline>FT-SE Eurotrack adds four companies, deletes four.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The FT-SE Eurotrack Indices Committee is to add Italy's Mediaset, France's Roussel Uclaf and SGS Thompson Micro, and Sweden's ABB &quot;B&quot; shares to the FT-SE Eurotrack 100 Index from September 23.</p>
<p>Four companies are being excluded: Italy's Montedison, France's Renault, Lyonnaise des Eaux SA and Lafarge Copee, FT-SE Eurotrack said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The next quarterly review will be held on December 12.</p>
<p>The indices are used in allocating fund assets and assessing risk and return.</p>
<p>-- David Chance London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
